&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Vercel is the agentic infrastructure company, freeing people and agents to ship what&#39;s next. For more than a decade we&#39;ve helped builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Now we&#39;re scaling our products for both agents and people to ship and run software, built in the open and trusted by OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Role:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vercel is looking for a Senior Recruiter to help us scale our Sales, Field Engineering, Partnerships, and other GTM and/or G&amp;amp;A functions as needed. You&#39;ll partner directly with business leaders and hiring managers on everything from steady, high-volume pipelines to senior, hard-to-fill searches.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll drive the full recruiting process for your functions: developing sourcing strategy, building pipelines of qualified passive candidates, running a rigorous and efficient interview process, and closing offers. You&#39;ll act as a consultative partner to your hiring managers, bringing market insight, calibration feedback, and clear recommendations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who is comfortable managing a full req load across multiple stakeholders, uses data to prioritize and to report on progress, and uses AI and recruiting technology to work more efficiently without compromising candidate experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is hybrid and based in one of our San Francisco or New York City,&amp;nbsp; with three in-office days per week (Monday, Tuesday, and Friday).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You Will Do:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own full-cycle recruiting for your assigned GTM functions, from search kickoff through offer acceptance, and take on new functions as hiring priorities change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with hiring managers to define role requirements, align on the hiring bar, and develop targeted sourcing strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain consistent, high-quality pipelines, including a focus on passive candidates, using direct outreach, referrals, networks, and communities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Screen candidates against clearly defined competencies and present hiring managers with well-qualified, calibrated slates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the interview process end to end, keeping candidates, interviewers, and hiring managers informed and moving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structure and negotiate offers in partnership with Compensation and other People teams, guiding candidates through to close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track pipeline metrics, report on progress and risk to hiring managers and recruiting leadership, and use the data to improve your process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 6+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience supporting go-to-market and/or technical roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve recruited in fast-paced, high-growth environments where hiring priorities shift quickly and speed matters without compromising quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve supported multiple functions or role types and can ramp on a new hiring profile efficiently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a track record of closing competitive candidates and managing offer processes from expectation-setting through acceptance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve built trusted relationships with hiring managers and can influence decisions on profile, process, and candidates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You source proactively and can point to hires generated through your own outreach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You use recruiting data and metrics to identify issues early, prioritize your work, and communicate clearly with stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You use or even build AI tools in your recruiting workflow and can describe where they&#39;ve improved your speed or quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Bonus If You:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have recruited for developer tools, infrastructure, or frontend technology companies with strong GTM functions, or are comfortable discussing frontend development, web performance, and cloud technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are familiar with Vercel&#39;s technology stack, competitive landscape, and market positioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have built recruiting processes and systems for GTM teams from the ground up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Competitive compensation package, including equity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Inclusive Healthcare Package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Learn and Grow - we provide mentorship and send you to events that help you build your network and skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Flexible Time Off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We will provide you the gear you need to do your role, and a WFH budget for you to outfit your space as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;The San Francisco, CA base salary range for this role is $176,000 - $215,000 plus annual bonus. Actual salary will be based on job-related skills, experience, and location. Compensation outside of San Francisco may be adjusted based on employee location. The total compensation package may include benefits, equity-based compensation, and eligibility for a company bonus or variable pay program depending on the role. Your recruiter can share more details during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
