&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About Vercel:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Vercel is the agentic infrastructure company, freeing people and agents to ship what&#39;s next. For more than a decade we&#39;ve helped builders move from idea to production with speed, security, and exceptional developer experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Now we&#39;re scaling our products for both agents and people to ship and run software, built in the open and trusted by OpenAI, PayPal, Ramp, Supreme, and millions of developers worldwide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About The Role:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vercel is hiring a &lt;strong&gt;Strategic Product Partnerships Lead&lt;/strong&gt; to develop first-of-a-kind partnerships that inflect the company&#39;s growth. Done well, these partnerships open distribution for our products, create new pipeline for our field teams, and/or add new capabilities to our platform. This is a highly cross-functional and technical role: you will spend as much time with product and engineering leaders as with commercial ones, both with partners and with Vercelians.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the Head of Strategic Partnerships and own a named set of partners that includes hyperscalers, frontier AI labs, silicon vendors, and commerce and enterprise software platforms. The work takes a different shape with each one, but the common thread is that these partnerships live close to the product: embedding Vercel inside a partner&#39;s platform, co-building new products, taking a joint offering to enterprises that neither company could sell alone. Structuring a deal means both understanding the technical components well enough to know what a partnership makes possible and understanding what the business impact could be if done successfully.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We expect candidates to demonstrate significant experience delivering complex deal work, creating and driving strategy, working with cross-functional teams to launch new initiatives, and initiating first-of-a-kind partnerships. We are looking for someone with a strong sense of ownership who performs at a senior level and does their best work with limited direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid position, requiring 3 days per week in one of our San Francisco, Austin, or New York City offices.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You Will Do:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a named set of strategic partners end to end, from first conversation through signed agreement to launch and growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and develop new partnerships with the companies that matter most to Vercel&#39;s strategy across AI, cloud, commerce, and enterprise software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the business case: size the opportunity, scope the product and engineering investment it requires, and give leadership a clear recommendation, including when the recommendation is to pass&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead negotiations end to end, structuring commercial agreements that are new to Vercel and often new to the partner: revenue share, embedded pricing, co-sell commitments, marketplace terms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop senior relationships on the partner side and bring Vercel executives in where the relationship calls for it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional teams across Product, Engineering, Sales, Marketing, Finance, and Legal to take a signed agreement to launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise Vercel leadership on where the ecosystem is moving and what it means for our roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run deals with structure: clear milestones, agreed measures of success on both sides, and the judgment to stop the ones that are not working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years developing, negotiating, and executing complex commercial agreements, ideally at a platform, infrastructure, cloud, or developer tools company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of initiating partnerships that had no precedent, with companies significantly larger than your own. You can walk through the terms you won and the ones you gave up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience structuring deals with significant technical surface area: platform integrations, embedded or whitelabeled product, licensing, infrastructure and compute commitments. You can hold a credible conversation with a partner&#39;s product and engineering teams about agents, inference, model routing, and cloud infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating and driving strategy, and getting an organization to fund it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable leading cross-functional teams you do not manage, through Product, Engineering, Legal, Finance, and Sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong agency and comfort with ambiguity. You decide what to work on and can defend the choice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Speed. You move quickly and decisively, and you keep large deals from stalling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication with executives on both sides of the table&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Bonus if you:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have done partnerships at or with a hyperscaler, a frontier AI lab, or a large commerce or enterprise software platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have structured technology licensing, OEM, or embedded distribution agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Started in a technical role (engineering, solutions architecture, or technical product) before moving into commercial work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Competitive compensation package, including equity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Inclusive Healthcare Package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Learn and Grow - we provide mentorship and send you to events that help you build your network and skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Flexible Time Off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;We will provide you the gear you need to do your role, and a WFH budget for you to outfit your space as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;The San Francisco, CA salary range for this role is $194,000 - $237,000, plus an annual company target bonus. Actual salary will be based on job-related skills, experience, and location. Compensation outside of San Francisco may be adjusted based on employee location. The total compensation package may include benefits, equity-based compensation, and eligibility for a company bonus or variable pay program depending on the role. Your recruiter can share more details during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
